Honour the documented FMA accumulation in the MoE combine (rollout patch 0004).
The header contracts that experts 1..k-1 accumulate with FMA; this build's
project-wide -ffp-contract=off silently made them round separately, which the
new tests/rocm/native_moe_combine_parity.cpp detected bit-for-bit. Rationale:
PORTING.md section 6n.
--- a/src/kernels/cuda/native_moe.cu
+++ b/src/kernels/cuda/native_moe.cu
@@ -38,7 +38,18 @@
     if (col >= n_embd) return;
     float sum = parts[col] * weights[0];
     for (int expert = 1; expert < k; ++expert) {
-        sum += parts[int64_t(expert) * n_embd + col] * weights[expert];
+        // Explicit rather than left to the compiler. The header contracts that
+        // experts 1..k-1 "accumulate with FMA in expert order"; this build sets
+        // -ffp-contract=off for every HIP translation unit (a deliberate choice,
+        // PORTING.md section 7), which made the same expression round the product
+        // separately instead. Measured before the fix: 35 to 280 of 256 to 512
+        // elements differed from the contracted reference, and the output matched
+        // the separately-rounded order bit for bit.
+        //
+        // Naming __fmaf_rn makes the documented accumulation hold whatever the
+        // contraction setting is, which is strictly more robust than depending on
+        // a compiler default that differs between nvcc and clang.
+        sum = __fmaf_rn(parts[int64_t(expert) * n_embd + col], weights[expert], sum);
     }
     if (shared) sum += shared[col];
     output[col] = sum;
